> Checking the theory

>> An exact path, including a flat GCV criterion

For the three-point example at any \(\lambda>0\), the rank-one formula yields

$$
\hat\beta=\frac1{1+6\lambda}(2\lambda,1+2\lambda,2\lambda),\quad
Q=\frac4{(1+6\lambda)^2},\quad
\operatorname{RSS}=\frac{24\lambda^2}{(1+6\lambda)^2},\quad
\operatorname{edf}=2+\frac1{1+6\lambda}.
$$
\alttext(The fitted coefficients, roughness, RSS and effective degrees of freedom are rational functions with common factor one plus six lambda.)

Substitution gives GCV = 2 and exact CV = 3 for *every positive lambda*.
This tiny dataset has no tuning information under either criterion; a flat score is
not evidence for a unique optimum. At lambda zero it interpolates and deletion is
unidentified, so both scores are reported as infinity rather than evaluating zero over zero.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pspline_exact_path.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const dm::Vector<> loglambda=dm::seql(-3,3,25), lambdas=dm::exp(loglambda*std::log(10.0));
  const auto path=dm::PSR::smoothing_path({0,1,2},{0,1,0},3,lambdas,1,2);
  const auto exact_edf=2+1/(1+6*lambdas);
  auto edf=dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), tradeoff=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  edf.lines(loglambda.values(),exact_edf.values(),"Exact",{70,70,70},3)
    .points(loglambda.values(),path.numeric_column("edf").values(),"Cholesky",{37,99,235},3)
    .title("Two line modes always survive").x_label("log10(lambda)").y_label("Effective df").y_limits(1.9,3.5);
  tradeoff.lines(loglambda.values(),path.numeric_column("roughness").values(),"Roughness Q",{220,90,35},3)
    .lines(loglambda.values(),path.numeric_column("rss").values(),"RSS",{37,99,235},3)
    .title("Roughness falls; training error rises").x_label("log10(lambda)").y_label("Squared response").y_limits(0,5.5);
  auto layout=dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2); layout.add(edf).add(tradeoff);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  layout.size(1100,490).fit_panels().save_svg("build/pspline_exact_path.svg");
  const auto error=dm::abs(dm::Vector<>(path.numeric_column("edf").values())-exact_edf);
  std::print("Maximum edf error against the closed form: {:.3e}\n\n",*std::max_element(error.begin(),error.end()));
  std::print("{}\n",dm::PSR::smoothing_path({0,1,2},{0,1,0},3,{.001,.1,1,10,1000},1,2).to_md(9));
}
```
